Test that the echo controller is made anew only when recording starts again

WebRTC's audio state with its patches 0009 and 0010, a mock audio device that keeps
whether it records and a mock audio processing: the echo controller is made anew at each
call's start (the first, and the next one starting with recording) and restarted for
recording once for the microphone on again with nothing else sending, never while a
shared screen's sound or another connection's voice comes and goes, nor when recording
fails to start. Built in again with the mocks: the library shows only its own API.

